Z||000000||JSocha||05-06-2001||02:34 PM||||Just broke her out of cold storage yesterday and she fired right up on the first shot and I'm not even mechanically inclined!  <P>I'm just so Happy I could just poop!<P>A 1995 Grasshopper 718K!<P>Completly Stock from the dealership:<P>1) 18HP Kohler OHV twin cylinder motor<BR>2) Air cooled<BR>3) Duel Hydrostatic independently controlled wheels...hence she turns literally on a dime!<BR>4) 15 Cubic foot storage capacity in the back<BR>5) Lowered 48" front deck<BR>6) 2 20x10.00-8NHS Goodyears on the front with factory rims<BR>7) 2 13x5.00-6 Cheng Shin Tires on the rear<BR>8) Front traction and weight control kit<BR>9) 13 Gallon Fuel tank<BR>10) PTO drive to optional accessories<BR>11) Engine overheat and Oil Sentry Protection for immidate shut down<BR>12) High quality/high shine headlights<BR>13) Three rotary's<BR>14) Blower with high volume capacity vacume tube<BR>15) Outstanding gas milage!  Whole day of driving on one tank of gas, from sunup to sunset!<P>And now folks, the moment you all have been waiting for as here is the picture of this stock beauty gem!<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/721D_thumb.gif">    <P>I can tell she is lookin forward to being driven another summer, as she's always been garaged and has never seen "rain" on her body and/or feet!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha.jpg">  <P>As you can tell, we North Dakotan's take pride in our lawn mowers as we have to!<P>Bring it on any of you Dixon owners as my Grasshopper eats em up and spits em out on the compost heap!<p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 05-07-2001).]||||reg||10
